A dramatic split composition in the style of Vincent van Gogh with bold, swirling brushstrokes and rich impasto textures. On the left side, a cascading waterfall of golden autumn leaves flows downward in a strict vertical stream, each leaf following the one before in perfect sequential order, painted with characteristic van Gogh yellows and oranges. On the right side, the same leaves are arranged in an organic branching tree structure, spreading outward like neural pathways or family trees, with deep blues and vibrant greens creating depth. Where the two sides meet in the center, individual leaves transform and blur between patterns, caught mid-transition. The background features van Gogh's iconic turbulent sky with concentric spiraling clouds in deep purples and electric blues, suggesting the cosmic nature of human thought. A crescent moon illuminates the scene from above, casting ethereal light on both organizational patterns equally.
